From d1e361bd1bec4bb78961956decfd886ae0282b26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:08:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(ui): the 3D tool preview shows helical flutes

The tool library window's 3D preview cuts helical grooves into the
fluted length of the revolved model: the stated flute count, twisted by
the catalog helix angle (straight when it is 0 or not stated). A Flutes
toggle stands after Dimensions and Holder (view state, starts on).

Display only: the fluted mesh is built in a private module of crates/ui;
the steel outline, the holder bands, the plain meshes and the tool's
envelope do not change with the flutes, and each fluted point lies
inside the revolved envelope. The fluted meshes are built with the rest
of the model on the same key; a still frame builds nothing.

Fixes #3908

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
